s>J</given-names></name><name><surname>Rudensey</surname><given-names>LM</given-names></name><name><surname>Papenhausen</surname><given-names>MD</given-names></name><name><surname>Benveniste</surname><given-names>RE</given-names></name><name><surname>Morton</surname><given-names>WR</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Variation in simian immunodeficiency virus <italic>env</italic> is confined to V1 and V4 during progression to simian AIDS</article-title><source>J Virol</source><year>1991</year><volume>65</volume><fpage>7025</fpage><lpage>7031</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">1942255</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B6"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Chackerian</surname><given-names>B</given-names></name><name><surname>Rudensey</surname><given-names>L</given-names></name><name><surname>Overbaugh</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Specific N-linked and O-linked glycosylation additions in the envelope V1 domain of SIV variants that evolve in the host alter neutralizing antibody recognition</article-title><source>J Virol</source><year>1997</year><volume>71</volume><fpage>7719</fpage><lpage>7727</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">9311856</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B7"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Rudensey</surname><given-names>LM</given-names></name><name><surname>Kimata</surname><given-names>JT</given-names></name><name><surname>Long</surname><given-names>EM</given-names></name><name><surname>Chackerian</surname><given-names>B</given-names></name><name><surname>Overbaugh</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Changes in the extracellular envelope glycoprotein of variants that evolve during the course of simian immunodeficiency virus SIVMne infection affect neutralizing antibody recognition, syncytium formation, and macrophage tropism but not replication, cyto